# Nuclear Project Quality Manager

Job Category:
Project Management / Controls

Contract Partner Company:
Equans

Employing Company:
Axima UK - Equans Group

The HPC Jobs Service supports local people into exciting, long-term careers across our Project.

**Nuclear Project Quality Manager**
**Equans**
**Hinkley Point C**

Rooted in more than a century of history, Equans, a Bouygues Group company, is the new global leader in energy and services. By supporting its customers through the energy, digital, and industrial transitions, Equans provides a high level of technical expertise in the design, installation, maintenance, and operation of multi-technical facilities.

Axima Nucléaire (950 employees, €217 million revenue in 2025), an Equans entity, is the European leader in nuclear ventilation and fluid process systems. With more than 50 years of experience, we offer comprehensive solutions ranging from engineering to maintenance for nuclear facilities. Our expertise covers new installations, modifications, and preparations for the decommissioning of nuclear sites.

As part of our continued growth, we are looking for our future:
Nuclear Project Quality Manager (M/F)

Based in London (UK) or Bristol (UK) or Lille (France)

**Your challenge with us:**

As part of the major UK nuclear projects Hinkley Point C (HPC) and Sizewell C (SZC), Axima Nucléaire is involved in the design, manufacturing, installation, and commissioning of HVAC systems and Emergency Diesel Generator (EDG) systems integrated into our clients' industrial facilities.

Reporting to the Quality and Supplier Oversight Department, you will be assigned to a project as Project Quality Manager for one of our contracts.

**Your main responsibilities will include:**

Ensuring that contractual quality requirements are fully integrated into the project's Management System and effectively implemented by all personnel, subcontractors, and the wider supply chain;
Establishing, maintaining, and managing the Contract Quality Assurance Plan (CQAP) through the implementation, maintenance, and continuous updating of the Project Quality Management System and all associated documentation (policies, procedures, guides, surveillance plans, registers, etc.);
Obtaining and maintaining ISO certifications for the Bristol entity in alignment with the global management system;
Coordinating the quality team for engineering and procurement activities, while providing oversight and project support for on-site installation activities;
Implementing independent quality and nuclear safety oversight through site inspections, internal and external audits, and regular site visits;
Managing subcontracted manufacturing inspection contracts in coordination with the Quality and Supplier Oversight Department;
Managing non-conformities by overseeing the related processes and tools, monitoring customer claims, and ensuring their effective resolution and closure;
Participating in selected supplier audits alongside Project Quality Engineers;
Collaborating with the department to share best practices and drive continuous improvement.

Travel within the United Kingdom and France will be required depending on the successful candidate's location.

**Requirements:**

You hold a Master's degree (Bac +5 equivalent) in Engineering or a related field.
Your expertise in Quality Assurance (QA) and Quality Control (QC), together with your knowledge of standards and frameworks such as ISO 19443 and IAEA GS-R-3, will be essential for success in this role.
Knowledge of UK nuclear quality standards, regulations, and practices (Licence Condition 17 (LC17) and/or Construction Design and Management Regulations (CDM)) would be a significant advantage.

**You are recognized for your:**

Rigour and attention to detail;
Ability to work autonomously;
Strong interpersonal and communication skills;
Cross-functional leadership and decision-making capabilities.
You are comfortable communicating on a daily basis in English.

For this role you must have evidence of right to work in the UK. As a project, we do not discriminate on the grounds of age, gender, race, colour, religion, disability or sexual orientation, and we welcome applications from all sections of the community.

