# staff full stack software engineer

Vacancy details

Canada|United States

Remote

Recruiter

Olesia Kravchenko

Olesia Kravchenko

o.kravchenko@svitla.com

## Role overview

Svitla Systems Inc. is looking for a Staff Full-Stack Software Engineer fora full-time position (40 hours per week).

We're looking for a Staff Full-Stack Software Engineer to help build and shape our cloud-based platform that brings together digital forensic tools, case management, evidence storage, and collaboration workflows to help investigators uncover critical evidence faster. You'll set technical direction across teams while staying hands-on across the stack, on a platform used by forensic investigators around the world.

This is a Staff-level role for experienced full-stack engineers who already lead a team's technical direction. You'll work alongside collaborative, customer-focused colleagues, mentor other engineers, and lead how our teams use AI-assisted development.

**NOTE: Candidates must reside in Canada or USA**

## 

Some of the tools and technologies used across our teams include:

* .NET / C#;
* AWS;
* React, TypeScript, HTML, CSS;
* REST and GraphQL APIs;
* Automated testing (e.g. xUnit, Jest, PyTest);
* Azure DevOps, GitLab, Git, and Jenkins;
* Python;
* Linux and shell scripting;
* Docker and containerized services (e.g. Kubernetes);
* Infrastructure-as-code (e.g. CDK);
* Distributed, message-driven systems;
* Elasticsearch and search/indexing systems;
* Prometheus, Grafana, and OpenTelemetry;
* AI coding tools such as Claude Code and Cursor.

## Requirements

* 10+ years of professional software engineering experience, most of it in full-stack roles spanning both front-end and back-end systems;
* Current or recent technical leadership as a Tech Lead, Staff engineer, or owner of a production system's core architecture, with a record of mentoring engineers;
* Post-secondary education in software engineering, computer or electrical engineering, computer science, math, or a related field, or equivalent experience;
* Experience building distributed systems and microservices for cloud-native SaaS products at scale;
* Deep expertise in C#/.NET server-side development (APIs, services, data access, performance tuning);
* Proficiency with React and modern front-end web development (component design, state management, responsive UI);
* Production experience with AWS;
* Working experience with Azure DevOps, Kubernetes and Linux environments;
* Active, everyday use of AI coding tools such as Claude Code or Cursor as part of your development workflow;
* Experience defining testing strategy and writing automated tests at various levels of abstraction;
* A track record of measurable impact on performance, reliability or security;
* Ability to work cross-functionally, communicate effectively with technical and non-technical stakeholders, and collaborate in a team environment;
* Comfortable navigating ambiguity and adapting in a fast-changing environment.

## Will be a plus

* Python or other programming languages;
* Shell scripting;
* Distributed data stores such as Elasticsearch, Redis, or PostgreSQL JSONB, and search/indexing systems;
* Observability and monitoring tools such as Prometheus, Grafana, or OpenTelemetry;
* Infrastructure-as-code (e.g. CDK) and container-based deployment pipelines;
* Distributed, message-driven systems and real-time features (e.g. WebSockets);
* Building integration platforms or partner APIs (REST, GraphQL);
* AI technologies in products, such as natural language search and agentic workflows;
* Experience in security-conscious or highly regulated environments, including handling sensitive data.

## Responsibilities

* Act as technical lead for our team: set technical direction, plan delivery and unblock engineers;
* Analyze requirements, break down cross-team initiatives, and provide effort estimates and sequencing;
